[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353530443","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111083#issuecomment-3353530443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111083","id":3353530443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H4tBL","user":{"login":"miruji","id":147953988,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNGZRA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147953988?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji","html_url":"https://github.com/miruji","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T19:33:31Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T19:36:20Z","body":"So, as I understand it, with a certain small chance, this can be done from any point of the slider, and it is not related to other GUI elements.\n\nBy the way, it seems to me that this has always been the case in previous versions. Most likely, it’s related to the fact that, for example, it’s specified as 0.0–1.0, but you can actually type any value through edit, and it will be accepted without issues. However, the slider itself is designed only for a specific range of values, which causes a bug where values outside the range are considered normal.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/49867ba5-dc7c-49c4-bfd5-9f66e5ba845b","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353530443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353623093","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111083#issuecomment-3353623093","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111083","id":3353623093,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H5Do1","user":{"login":"boss2412","id":146807191,"node_id":"U_kgDOCMAZlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146807191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boss2412","html_url":"https://github.com/boss2412","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boss2412/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boss2412/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boss2412/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boss2412/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boss2412/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boss2412/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boss2412/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boss2412/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boss2412/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T20:05:28Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T20:05:28Z","body":"Where exactly should i look for the bug in Repository.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3353623093/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3355216936","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111083#issuecomment-3355216936","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111083","id":3355216936,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7H_Iwo","user":{"login":"miruji","id":147953988,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNGZRA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147953988?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji","html_url":"https://github.com/miruji","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-01T08:07:47Z","updated_at":"2025-10-01T08:07:47Z","body":"> Where exactly should i look for the bug in Repository.\n\nI think this applies to any slider in the editor that has value limits, but where you can manually enter a number greater than the limit. Or as shown in the video and described above.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3355216936/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358473405","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111083#issuecomment-3358473405","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111083","id":3358473405,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ILjy9","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-01T23:15:03Z","updated_at":"2025-10-01T23:15:03Z","body":"This is intended behavior. Sliding through the slider is limited, though sliding the number itself (not the slider)/ typing any number works fine, this is because some properties use the or_greater/or_less argument for `PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE` hint.\nFor more info check `PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE` constant of [`PropertyHint`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_@globalscope.html#enum-globalscope-propertyhint), check also [`@export_range()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_@globalscope.html#enum-globalscope-propertyhint).\n\nYou can make such property yourself by pasting the following into any gdscript attached to a node and inspecting that node's properties:\n```gdscript\n@export_range(0, 1, .01) var normal = 0.0\n@export_range(0, 1, .01, \"or_less\") var undershoot = 0.0\n@export_range(0, 1, .01, \"or_greater\") var overshoot = 0.0\n@export_range(0, 1, .01, \"or_greater\", \"or_less\") var can_do_anything = 0.0\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358473405/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3362414010","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111083#issuecomment-3362414010","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111083","id":3362414010,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ial26","user":{"login":"miruji","id":147953988,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNGZRA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147953988?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji","html_url":"https://github.com/miruji","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miruji/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-02T18:12:15Z","updated_at":"2025-10-02T18:12:15Z","body":"> This is intended behavior. Sliding through the slider is limited, though sliding the number itself (not the slider)/ typing any number works fine, this is because some properties use the or_greater/or_less argument for `PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE` hint. For more info check `PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE` constant of [`PropertyHint`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_@globalscope.html#enum-globalscope-propertyhint), check also [`@export_range()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_@globalscope.html#enum-globalscope-propertyhint).\n\nThank you for the explanation. I understand the expected behavior with or_less / or_greater, but then what is the point of limiting the values in the editor if they can still exceed the range?\n\nEither it should be restricted not only for the slider but also for manual input, or it should be unrestricted for the slider as well as for manual input, or it can stay as it is now — but in that case it really looks like a bug, even though I could understand such a “hybrid” approach (meaning it would be fine if this hybrid didn’t come with the kind of bug shown in the video).\n\nThere are situations where having a limit but being able to go beyond it could make sense, but I’m not sure if this is well represented in the current form — and I wonder if something might break if, for example, I set a value like 19000 just because I can.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3362414010/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3362481019","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111083#issuecomment-3362481019","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111083","id":3362481019,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ia2N7","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-02T18:32:53Z","updated_at":"2025-10-02T18:32:53Z","body":"> what is the point of limiting the values in the editor if they can still exceed the range?\n\nThis is an optional feature for ranges where you might recommended to the user tol be in range between x,y. Although this is usually used to prevent entering negative numbers where one would expect only positive numbers (Which is the case with `OmniLight3D.size`)\n\nBut assuming you now understand the intention, I think this Issue can now be closed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3362481019/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]